From 523bb9601442ad9b1287e2dae362203489e9055f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 09:59:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Reuse a native LODF context across outage chunks for full
 N-1 performance

Chunking on the Python side previously called the stateless native LODF
per chunk, reloading the network and refactorizing the DC Jacobian each
time (~178 ms per chunk on case9241pegase). Add a handle-based native API
(create_lodf_matrix_context / compute_lodf_matrix_from_context /
free_lodf_matrix_context) backed by LodfComputer.Context, which loads and
factorizes once. compute_lodf_matrix now creates one context, computes all
chunks against it, and frees it, cutting per-chunk overhead to ~32 ms
(matrix marshaling only) - matching the performance of a single
in-process computation.

