Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 12:47:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Expose thread_count in the pypowsybl LODF API (Phase 2
 multithreading)

Thread the LODF threadCount through the native LODF entry points (one-shot
and from-context), the C++ wrappers, the pybind11 bindings and the Python
compute_lodf_matrix. The factor fill is parallelized across outaged
branches while the result stays identical whatever the thread count.
Verified from Python: thread_count 2 and 4 give bit-identical results and
speed up the fill (16049 x 2000 on case9241pegase: 3.8 s -> 2.2 s on 4
threads).

